{"name":"Prayer Flag","hex":"#d59c6a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prayer flag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colourful rectangular cloth hung from a thread and strung along mountain ridges and peaks high in the Himalayas by practitioners of Tibetan Buddhism to bless the surrounding countryside or for other purposes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prayer_flag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prayer flag","blocks":[{"text":"A Tibetan prayer flag is a colorful rectangular cloth, often found strung along trails and peaks high in the Himalayas. They are used to bless the surrounding countryside and for other purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Prayerflags.jpg/330px-Prayerflags.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prayer_flag","wikidata":"Q1422079"},{"title":"Prayer","blocks":[{"text":"Prayer is an invocation or act that seeks to activate a rapport with an object of worship through deliberate communication. In the narrow sense, the term refers to an act of supplication or intercession directed towards a deity or a deified ancestor. More generally, prayer can also have the purpose of giving thanks or praise, and in comparative religion is closely associated with more abstract forms of meditation and with charms or spells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Prayers-collage.png/330px-Prayers-collage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prayer","wikidata":"Q40953"},{"title":"Flag","blocks":[{"text":"A flag is a piece of fabric with distinctive colours and design, often flown from a pole and used for symbolic, signalling, or decorative purposes. The term flag is also used to refer to the graphic design employed on such pieces of fabric. The study of flags is known as \"vexillology\" from the Latin vexillum, meaning \"flag\" or \"banner\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/United_Nations_Flags_-_cropped.jpg/330px-United_Nations_Flags_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag","wikidata":"Q14660"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Waddell-p411-The-Tibetan-LUNG-Horse.jpg/330px-Waddell-p411-The-Tibetan-LUNG-Horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Waddell-p411-The-Tibetan-LUNG-Horse.jpg/330px-Waddell-p411-The-Tibetan-LUNG-Horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Tibetan \"lung ta\" or \"wind horse\" from an 1895 book by Laurence Austine Waddell","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWaddell-p411-The-Tibetan-LUNG-Horse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Praying_Germanic_man_1890.jpg/330px-Praying_Germanic_man_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Praying_Germanic_man_1890.jpg/330px-Praying_Germanic_man_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A kneeling position with raised hands expressed \"supplication\" in classical antiquity. The word for \"prayer\" and for \"supplication\" is identical in ancient languages (oratio, προσευχή, תְּפִלָּה etc.), with no terminological distinction between supplications addressed to human as opposed to divine powers.\nStatuette known as \"Praying German\" or \"supplicating barbarian\". It is not known if this figure was originally set in a context of religious prayer or of military surrender.[22]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APraying_Germanic_man_1890.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Ring48.jpg/500px-Ring48.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Ring48.jpg/500px-Ring48.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The valkyrie Sigrdrífa says a pagan Norse prayer in Sigrdrífumál; illustration by Arthur Rackham","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARing48.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Theophile_Lybaert_-_Old_Flanders.jpeg/500px-Theophile_Lybaert_-_Old_Flanders.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Theophile_Lybaert_-_Old_Flanders.jpeg/500px-Theophile_Lybaert_-_Old_Flanders.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old woman praying by Théophile Lybaert","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATheophile_Lybaert_-_Old_Flanders.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Schnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_136.png/500px-Schnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_136.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Schnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_136.png/500px-Schnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_136.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"David Prays for Deliverance, 1860 woodcut by Julius Schnorr von Karolsfeld","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchnorr_von_Carolsfeld_Bibel_in_Bildern_1860_136.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Muro_de_las_Lamentaciones%2C_Jerusal%C3%A9n%2C_2017.gif/500px-Muro_de_las_Lamentaciones%2C_Jerusal%C3%A9n%2C_2017.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip